# Runtime log the program writes beside itself
tdstoolkit.log
tdstoolkit.log.*

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/

# PyInstaller. The exe goes to a Release, not into the repository - but
# the spec is the recipe it is built from and is edited by hand, so it
# is kept. Nothing regenerates it.
build/
dist/
*.spec
!TDS Toolkit.spec

tdstoolkit.json

# Runtime state the program writes beside itself: the upload manifest
# (skip-unchanged), the per-instrument transfer outcome (failure lock-out),
# and the single-process lock.
tdstoolkit-uploads.json
tdstoolkit-transfers.json
tdstoolkit.lock

# Bench scripts and one-shot probes. Useful to have, not part of the
# program - and _to_delete is a staging area, not a folder to keep.
scratch/
_to_delete/

# Private bench note, kept local and out of the repo.
MEMORY-TEST-NOTES.md

# --- Private bench material (kept local, never published) ---
# The dev test harness and its fixtures, the bench tools, the captured
# reference waveforms, the manual sources, worked bench examples, and the
# private working notes. All of this lives on the maintainer's machine and
# is deliberately out of the public repository. See CLAUDE.md.
tests/
tools/
waves/
examples/
docs/manual/
notes/
sample.wfm

# Runtime folder the app writes beside itself for saved limit-test masks.
limits/

# --- Internal/dev docs: kept on disk, deliberately not published ---
# Design and reverse-engineering notes, the maintainer guide, the 68k
# helper source (its assembled bytes are embedded in tds_fw.py), and the
# decoder-authoring aids. None are needed to use the app. See the private
# tools/ and notes/ for the rest of the maintainer-only material.
/CLAUDE.md
/FILE-TRANSFER-AUDIT.md
/FILE-TRANSFER-HARDENING.md
/fwhelper.S
/docs/TDS Toolkit - Writing a Protocol Decoder.pdf
/decoders/_template.py
/decoders/README.txt
